### Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1** – *Navigate to Storage* | Move from the current position to the storage location where the resource is kept. | AND (to G4) | `Storage` | `[1,∞]` | Multiple robots can perform this action in parallel when several storages are involved. |
| **AT2** – *Send Request to Storage* | Transmit a message to the storage system specifying the exact resources required. | AND (to G5) | `Storage` | `1` | Only the robot that has arrived at the storage needs to send the request. |
| **AT3** – *Wait for Resource Retrieval* | Remain at the storage until the requested items are physically retrieved. | AND (to G6) | `Storage` | `1` | The robot that requested the resource must wait for it. |
| **AT4** – *Return to Recharge Station* | Move to the nearest recharging station to replenish the battery. | AND (to G7) | `RechargeStation` | `1` | Only the robot that is low on battery needs to recharge. |
| **AT5** – *Assign Mission to Another Robot* | Notify the central controller (or a peer robot) that the mission has to be handed over. | AND (to G7) | `ControlCenter` | `1` | The robot that is recharging must inform another robot to take over. |
| **AT6** – *Transport Resource to Destination* | Carry the resource from the storage (or checkpoint) to the final destination. | AND (to G8) | `Destination` | `[1,∞]` | Several robots can transport different resources concurrently. |
| **AT7** – *Return Resource to Checkpoint* | Bring the resource back to a predefined checkpoint before handing it over. | AND (to G10) | `Checkpoint` | `1` | The robot that is low on battery must return the resource. |
| **AT8** – *Assign Remaining Delivery Task to Another Robot* | Inform another robot of the remaining delivery run and its destination. | AND (to G12) | `ControlCenter` | `1` | The robot that has returned to the checkpoint must hand over the rest of the task. |
| **AT9** – *Send Alert to Sector Manager* | Generate an alert that the robot failed to return the resource to a checkpoint. | AND (to G11) | `ControlCenter` | `1` | The robot that cannot return to the checkpoint must trigger an alert. |

